# ::tok I personally think it 's acceptable . Firstly , the price is cheap , and the 700 + pages are divided into two books , which are also easy to flip through as paperback ; secondly , unlike the complete works of Michelangelo , the paintings are the main part , and the black and white manuscripts of Da Vinci make up the majority . For readers with limited budgets and non - art majors , this version has the highest cost - performance ratio for appreciating paintings and manuscripts .
